      "writtenOn": "2022-07-08T14:13:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, it\u0027s no wonder that this is broken: I\u0027ve been very much in doubt about what little- and big-endian even means when you\u0027re talking about non-byte-aligned fields 😄\n\nYou say this is documented, but where? The best pointer is from David who sent me to your new Python code for this (which I should read and port to Rust).",
